      "closure_rationale": "The original checked/wrapping/saturating policies and bounded intermediate derivation remain distinct from RFC1982 admissible serial increments. Width2..16 comparison preserves output at exact half-range and delegates16bits to actual er_serial16. The finite4bit relation has336oriented three-cycles, including0>11>6>0; antisymmetry on comparable pairs does not imply transitivity or a valid unrestricted sorting comparator. An actual four-entry window queue preflights every resident age before advancing, including overdue items, preserving control/output on refusal. Since age and initial delay remain below half-range, integer age-delay gives an unambiguous common live window; pop selects oldest due with stable insertion ties. The API requires externally certified elapsed intervals, not an inference from two low samples, and duplicate/capacity behavior is exact. Six profiles execute6anchors,8compiled controls and6compiling-stub rejections. Independent integer timelines check324policy,417serial,70263window and1875absolute cases/profile; the4bit pair/triple model checks antisymmetry and exposes336cycles. Actual ER_MUTANT13/14 are rejected separately. Four actual GCC/Clang C23 executions show raw ckd_add overflow writes wrapped0 while staged publication preserves91 and operand side effects occur once. N3096 draft and installed headers are not published C23 inspection. The required delayed support implements a separate absolute uint64 timestamp queue: low display widths do not determine eligibility, so absolute1 overdue at16 and absolute17 future remain distinct despite equal low deadline1. Residence may cross many display wraps within the finite nonwrapping lifetime; checked exhaustion refuses new positive advancement without blocking due-item drain. A larger wrapping type alone is explicitly insufficient. Width/lifetime proofs, external elapsed authority and eventual reset recovery remain stated assumptions rather than invented physical measurements. Bounded author support only."
